Template: glitchtip/dbconfig-install
Type: boolean
Default: true
_Description: Configure database for glitchtip with dbconfig-common?
 The glitchtip package must have a database installed and configured
 before it can be used. This can be optionally handled with
 dbconfig-common.
 .
 If you are an advanced database administrator and know that you want
 to perform this configuration manually, you should refuse this option.
 Details on what needs to be done should most likely be provided in
 /usr/share/doc/glitchtip.
 .
 Otherwise, you should probably choose this option.

Template: glitchtip/pgsql/method
Type: select
Choices: ${choices}
_Description: Database installation method for glitchtip:
 The glitchtip package can be configured to use one of two
 different database types for its database. The default choice will
 use dbconfig-common instead, configuring the database automatically
 for you, though you can also connect to a database you manage yourself.
 .
 If you choose to connect to a database that you already manage, you
 need to have prepared this database and populated it with the
 correct database schema already.

Template: glitchtip/pgsql/authmethod-admin
Type: select
Choices: ident, password
Default: ident
_Description: Authentication method to use with PostgreSQL for glitchtip:
 The following methods are available for authenticating database
 access with your PostgreSQL server, for the administrator account.

Template: glitchtip/pgsql/authmethod-user
Type: select
Choices: ident, password
Default: ident
_Description: Authentication method to use with PostgreSQL for glitchtip:
 The following methods are available for authenticating database
 access with your PostgreSQL server, for the user account.

Template: glitchtip/db/dbname
Type: string
Default: glitchtip
_Description: Name of your database's administrative user:
 Please provide the name of the database's administrative user.

Template: glitchtip/db/app-user
Type: string
Default: glitchtip
_Description: Name of the database's user:
 Please specify the name of the database's user.

Template: glitchtip/pgsql/admin-user
Type: string
Default: postgres
_Description: Name of the database's admin user:
 Please specify the account that will be used for database
 administration.

Template: glitchtip/remote/host
Type: string
_Description: Remote host name:
 Please provide the hostname or IP address of the database server
 you want to connect to.

Template: glitchtip/remote/port
Type: string
_Description: Remote database port:
 Please provide the port used to connect to the database, if it is
 not the default port for your database type.

Template: glitchtip/purge
Type: boolean
Default: false
_Description: Do you want to purge the database when the package is removed?
 Please choose whether the database installed by dbconfig-common
 should be removed when the package is purged.
 .
 This choice only has effect if the database is on this host, and if
 dbconfig-common is handling the database installation.
 